# Excludes files from the Docker build context (what `docker build .` copies into the image
# via `COPY . /src`). Like .gitignore, but for image builds — keeps the image small and, more
# importantly, keeps secrets (.env) and the large ADS jars out of it.
#
# Must live at the build-context root (the repo root), because the gateway build context IS
# the repo root: the image pip-installs the SDK, which needs pyproject.toml + the package
# source here. The Dockerfile itself lives under examples/gateway/ (referenced via -f).
.venv/
.git/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
examples/policies/*.jar
examples/policies/*.license
**/.env
*.log
